{
  "text": "A new school year does not start in the same season everywhere. Summer holidays have different lengths, too. Let us look around the world. In Japan, school starts in spring, in early April. The year ends the next spring, in late March. The summer holiday lasts about six weeks. It comes during the school year, from late July to the end of August. Even in the USA, states have different rules and schools have different dates. In Anchorage, Alaska, school usually starts in late summer, in August. It ends in late spring, in May. The summer holiday lasts about eleven weeks. In Miami-Dade, Florida, school also starts in late summer, around the middle of August. It ends in early summer, in early June. The summer holiday is about ten weeks long. In Kent, England, the year usually starts in early autumn, around September 1. It ends in summer, in late July. The summer holiday lasts about six weeks. Dates can change from school to school. In UAE public schools, the year usually starts in late summer, near the end of August. It ends in summer, around July 1. The summer holiday lasts about eight weeks. In Jersey, the year usually starts in early autumn, in early September. It ends in summer, in July. The summer holiday lasts about seven weeks. In Anchorage, the school year runs for about nine months. In Kent, it runs for about eleven months. Both include short holidays. In Japan, the year goes from one spring to the next, with holidays along the way.",
